(353, 'giant-elk', 'Giant Elk', 'Гигантский лось', 'huge', 'beast', 14, 42, '5d12', 'walk 60 ft.', 16, 2, '2', 450, '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '[{"name":"Ram","desc":"Melee Weapon Attack: +6 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) bludgeoning damage.","attack_bonus":6,"damage":"2d6+4 bludgeoning"},{"name":"Hooves","desc":"Melee Weapon Attack: +6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one prone creature. Hit: 22 (4d8 + 4) bludgeoning damage.","attack_bonus":6,"damage":"4d8+4 bludgeoning"}]', 'The majestic giant elk is rare to the point that its appearance is often taken as a foreshadowing of an important event, such as the birth of a king. Legends tell of gods that take the form of giant elk when visiting the Material Plane. Many cultures therefore believe that to hunt these creatures is to invite divine wrath.', 'https://www.dnd5eapi.co/api/2014/monsters/giant-elk', 'https://5e14.dnd.su/bestiary/353-giant-elk/', 0),
(355, 'giant-fire-beetle', 'Giant Fire Beetle', 'Гигантский огненный жук', 'small', 'beast', 13, 4, '1d6', 'walk 30 ft.', 10, 0, '0', 10, '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '[{"name":"Bite","desc":"Melee Weapon Attack: +1 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 2 (1d6 - 1) slashing damage.","attack_bonus":1,"damage":"1d6-1 slashing"}]', 'A giant fire beetle is a nocturnal creature that takes its name from a pair of glowing glands that give off light. Miners and adventurers prize these creatures, for a giant fire beetle’s glands continue to shed light for 1d6 days after the beetle dies. Giant fire beetles are most commonly found underground and in dark forests.', 'https://www.dnd5eapi.co/api/2014/monsters/giant-fire-beetle', 'https://5e14.dnd.su/bestiary/355-giant-fire-beetle/', 0),
